 1.What is the difference between Shift Left Testing and Shift Right Testing?

Shift Left Testing means moving testing activities earlier in the software development lifecycle (SDLC).
Testing starts during requirement and design phase instead of waiting until development is completed.

Example:
Reviewing requirements
Writing test cases early
Unit testing by developers
Automation testing during development
Goal:
Find defects early and reduce cost.

Shift Right Testing means testing after the application is deployed in the production environment.
Focuses on real user behavior, monitoring, and performance.

Example:
Production monitoring
User feedback analysis
A/B testing
Performance monitoring
Error tracking
Goal:
Improve user experience and system reliability.

2.Explain about continuous Testing.
Continuous Testing is the process of executing automated tests continuously throughout the software development lifecycle to get fast feedback on quality and business risks.
It is mainly used in DevOps and Agile environments.
